When the BCCI named India’s squad for the tour of Zimbabwe, Prabhsimran Singh was one of three uncapped players selected. With Sanju Samson already locked in for the Asian Games later this year, it opened the door for Prabhsimran to replace him and be tried out as India's second wicketkeeper behind Ishan Kishan. And with Shreyas Iyer, his captain at Punjab Kings, leading the side, the transition to the national setup should be a smooth one for him to handle.
